    "prompt": "Use case stylized-concept. Original fan-made detailed pixel-art 2D sprite sheet of a MIST UNIT SKULL from Metal Gear Solid V The Phantom Pain (NOT Skull Face, not armor-rock variant). Faithful exposed bald pale-gray veiny head with small stenciled 02, inhuman cyan glowing eyes, black respirator covering mouth and nose with TWO vertical filters, black earmuff communications headset, thick circular black high gorget neck guard. Lean muscular male build in dark charcoal segmented tactical bodysuit and shoulder pads, harness pouches, knee pads, dark combat boots, compact bullpup rifle. No skull helmet or visible bare teeth, no stone armor, no human hair. Match in-game Where Do the Bees Sleep Skulls cinematic. EXACT4columns×4rows16 completely separate authored fullbody animation phases. Thin purecyan gridlines, pure#FF00FF flat background; generous 18% cell margins including gun. Side orthographic profile RIGHT, ONE consistent scale and groundbaseline, crisp pixel clusters. Row1 idle: four tense breathing and small head-scan phases. Row2 move: four deliberate stalking steps with genuinely alternating legs. Row3 attack: raise bullpup, aim, fire with small yellow muzzle flash, recoil. Row4 reaction: flinch, low defensive brace, recover, stand. Keep very small cyan mist wisps only immediately around boots, never fill background and never cross cells. No text captions, labels, UI, scenery, ground shadow, watermark. Each entire body and rifle inside its own cell, 16 independent drawings not duplicate translations.",
